  "traps": [
    "TE 5 spans 5 LANDSCAPE pages after a portrait cover; the two-row column header (group header \"REAL PROPERTY DATA (GFEBS, AS OF 30 SEP 2026)\" over CATCODE..GSF) is repeated on every page and must not be read as data.",
    "Running header (solicitation number, TE title), \"CUI\" banners top and bottom, and the footer \"Section J, Attachment 0003 | TE 5 – Page x of y | Issued 18 SEP 2026\" repeat on every page; the renderer adds a second overall \"Page n of m\" footer.",
    "Zone grouping rows (e.g. \"CANTONMENT AREA A – MAIN POST AND GARRISON HEADQUARTERS\", plus \"(CONTINUED)\" rows at page tops) are not facilities.",
    "Four zone SUBTOTAL rows (CANTONMENT AREA A 484,331; CANTONMENT AREA B 919,655; CANTONMENT AREA C 565,502; KAAF AND RANGE CONTROL 357,770) and a GRAND TOTAL row (2,327,258 GSF, 104 facilities) are not facilities; per General Note 4 they include the two demolition rows.",
    "T-2308 (ADMINISTRATIVE GENERAL PURPOSE (WWII WOOD), 4,712 GSF) and T-2314 (RESERVE COMPONENT TRAINING ROOM (WWII WOOD), 3,960 GSF) are marked \"DEMO FY27 – EXCLUDE\" in the CUSTODIAL FREQ column with footnote 2/ on the name: excluded, so truth has 102 facilities out of 104 listed rows.",
    "Footnote markers are superscripts glued to numbers, so the text layer shows e.g. \"61,4501/\" for 00207 (61,4501/), 00238 (14,2103/), 01245 (46,8001/), 02322 (72,0001/), 02324 (54,6001/), 04005 (104,3003/), 04007 (118,6403/), 04011 (11,7603/): GSF is the number without the marker. Name markers (2/, 4/, 5/) follow facility names.",
    "19 GSF values are printed without thousands separators (e.g. 7315, 3180, 9950) while the rest use commas; values under 1,000 (960, 860) are also present.",
    "Facility numbers mix formats: \"P-114\" (permanent prefix), \"00205\" and its annex \"00205A\" (distinct records, both in scope), \"T-2310\" (temporary; in scope) next to demolition rows T-2308 and T-2314, \"S-2340\", and range facilities \"R-5101\".",
    "Adjacent numeric columns YR BUILT | FLRS | GSF (e.g. \"1958 3 48,620\") must not be merged; the year is not square footage and FLRS is the floor count.",
    "CUSTODIAL FREQ maps 7X/WK → daily_7, 5X/WK → daily_5, 3X/WK → 3x_week, 2X/WK → 2x_week, 1X/WK → weekly. 1X/MO has no matching service level, so truth omits serviceLevel for T-2312, 02326, R-5125, R-5127, R-5130 (still in scope).",
    "Twin rows with identical data (01203/01204 battalion HQs, 01205/01206 COFs, 01210/01212/01214 and 01216/01218 UEPH barracks) are separate facilities and must all be kept.",
    "Footnotes 3/ (fire stations, hangars: bays excluded), 4/ (dining: kitchen by food service contractor) and 5/ (barracks: common areas only) limit custodial area but give no cleanable SF, so truth carries gross SF only and no cleanableSqft.",
    "Category is asserted only where the CATCODE description is unambiguous (e.g. 72111 → barracks, 72210 → dining, 21110 → hangar, 61050/1418x → admin); fire, MP, tower, terminal, bathhouse, fuel, range and youth-center codes carry no category.",
    "TE 6 Table 6-1 has a two-row header (IMPROVED (TYPE I) / SEMI-IMPROVED (TYPE II) / UNIMPROVED (TYPE III), each ACRES | MOWS/YR): acreage and mowing counts alternate (\"18.4 30 3.2 12 —\") and the MOWS/YR integers are not acres. \"—\" means none. Totals: Type I 126.6 AC, Type II 180.3 AC, Type III 611.0 AC; the TOTAL row is excluded.",
    "Grounds areas list their FACILITIES SERVED by TE 5 facility number; truth carries those as buildingNumbers. GC-1 and GD-2 give a text description instead of numbers, and GC-2 / GX-1 show \"—\", so those have no buildingNumbers.",
    "Table 6-2 playing fields (PF-1, 14.6 AC) are maintained to Type I standard but are explicitly not included in Table 6-1 Type I acreage: athletic_field, not improved_turf, and not double counted.",
    "Table 6-3 paved areas are in square yards (SY): parking 183,510 SY (= 1,651,590 SF) across PV-1..PV-4, sidewalks 27,600 SY (= 248,400 SF) in PV-5; the TOTAL PAVED AREA row (211,110 SY) is excluded. Truth keeps sqyd (the scorer converts)."
  ]
